592186345956 1100 "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩$ at the point where $t=0.$" 13194139535364 true] [17592186345956 1113 #uuid "927bdcac-2749-5a1c-8331-70b709fa149b" 13194139535364 true] [17592186345956 1145 "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨-{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,-{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0),\\,-{e}^{-(0)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-0+1,\\,-1-0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535364 true] [17592186345957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345958 13194139535364 true] [17592186345957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345959 13194139535364 true] [17592186345957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345960 13194139535364 true] [17592186345957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345961 13194139535364 true] [17592186345957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345962 13194139535364 true] [17592186345957 1040 #edb/r